/*!
\group harmonyos
\title Qt for HarmonyOS
\brief Provides information about HarmonyOS support in Qt.
\ingroup supportedplatform

\note Qt for HarmonyOS is in technology preview and may change in future
releases.

Qt for HarmonyOS enables you to develop Qt applications for HarmonyOS devices.

Qt for HarmonyOS provides the platform integration, build and packaging support,
and the platform plugin that connect the cross-platform Qt libraries (such as Qt
Core, Qt GUI, Qt Quick, and Qt Widgets) to HarmonyOS. A Qt application is
packaged into a HarmonyOS Ability Package (HAP) and runs on the device through
the HarmonyOS platform plugin.

\section1 Key features and capabilities

\list
\li \b{Cross-platform development.} Write your application code once, typically
    a Qt Quick application with a C++ back-end, and deploy it on HarmonyOS
    alongside the other platforms that Qt supports, with minimal or no
    adjustments.
\li \b{Native performance.} The Qt runtime is compiled for HarmonyOS, so it runs
    as native code on the device.
\li \b{Rich UI components.} Use \l{Qt Quick} and \l{Qt Quick Controls} for
    responsive interfaces, or \l{Qt Widgets} for traditional widget-based UIs.
\li \b{C++ integration.} Reuse existing C++ libraries and high-performance
    native code.
\endlist

\section1 Explore Qt for HarmonyOS

To learn about developing with Qt for HarmonyOS, see the following topics:

\list
    \li \l {Qt for HarmonyOS Prerequisites}
    \li \l {Qt for HarmonyOS - Building from Source}
    \li \l {Building and Deploying Qt Applications for HarmonyOS}
    \li \l {Qt for HarmonyOS CMake API}
    \li \l {The harmonyostestrunner Tool}
\endlist

\section1 Supported configurations

Building and developing with Qt for HarmonyOS is only supported on a Linux
development host. The following target architectures are supported:

\table
\header \li Architecture \li Target
\row \li \c arm64-v8a \li Physical devices
\row \li \c x86_64 \li Emulator
\endtable
*/
